    <Layer queryable="0" opaque="0" cascaded="0">
        <Name>msfTS</Name>
        <Title>Forecasts of Unusually Wet and Dry conditions (Multi-system)</Title>
        <Abstract>This layer provides an early warning of persistent extreme wet and dry precipitation events over Europe derived from 1-, 3-, and 6-month Standardized Precipitation Index (SPI1, SPI3 and SPI6 respectively). The forecasts of SPI are derived from the forecasted of precipitation provided by the ECMWF probabilistic seasonal model (S5). The early warning is plotted only when and where the forecast is considered robust (with at least 40% of the ensemble members associated with extreme forecasts) and associated with relative extreme values (SPI lower than -1). The colors indicate the return period of the intensity and the coherency of the ensemble members of the forecast model according to the reference period that spans from 1981 to 2010.</Abstract>
