      <Layer queryable="0" opaque="0" cascaded="0">
        <Name>rdria</Name>
        <Title>Risk of Drought Impact for Agriculture</Title>
        <Abstract>The Risk of Drought Impact for Agriculture (RDrI-Agri) is a categorized risk index, indicating the probability of having impacts from a drought, with particular focus on vegetation. Formerly known as Likelihood of Drought Impact (LDI), it differs from the latter in that soil moisture anomaly is included and the index is updated every ten days, instead of eight. It is a dynamic theme, updated every ten days.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;The RDrI-Agri combines drought hazard, drought exposure (i.e. the total population, its livelihoods and assets in an area in which drought events may occur), vulnerability (i.e. the propensity of exposed elements to suffer adverse effects when impacted by a drought event) and hazard. Drought hazard is expressed as the combination of rainfall anomaly (SPI, Standardized Precipitation Index), anomaly of the photosynthetic activity of the vegetation cover (fAPAR anomaly - fraction of Absorbed Photosynthetically Active Radiation Anomaly) and soil moisture anomalies.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Resolution is one decimal degree.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;More details in &lt;a target='_ref' href='https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0959378016300565'&gt;Carr&amp;atilde;o, H., Naumann, G., Barbosa, P., 2016. Mapping global patterns of drought risk: An empirical framework based on sub-national estimates of hazard, exposure and vulnerability. Global Environ. Change 39: 108-124.&lt;/a&gt;.</Abstract>
        <SRS>EPSG:4326</SRS>
        <SRS>EPSG:3035</SRS>
        <SRS>EPSG:900913</SRS>
        <SRS>EPSG:3857</SRS>
        <LatLonBoundingBox minx="-180.000000" miny="-90.000000" maxx="180.000000" maxy="90.000000"/>
        <BoundingBox SRS="EPSG:4326" minx="-180.000000" miny="-90.000000" maxx="180.000000" maxy="90.000000"/>
        <Dimension name="time" units="ISO8601"/>
        <Extent name="time" nearestValue="0">2010-01-01/2026-10-11/P10D</Extent>
